pr_comments:
@andyross @keith-packard thanks for your reviews.
I took all your input in. Wrt to #74700 I also took the test and the idea of checking that there was no .ctrs or .init_array left behind.
The test, will only be included if the feature is enabled though.

@andyross
I ended up placing the code in the kernel side. Just merged all those 3 init files into one.
I left the destructors file in the cpp library. It just provides an empty hook override for all but the native/posix arch targets. And even though `attribute(__destructor__)` also exists, and would need the same logic if supported, it makes little sense for Zephyr.

> Or a kconfig that defaults to y and let people sensitive to size set it to n if they can?

Given your proposal of checking at link time that there is nothing left behind, it actually seems nicer to leave it disabled. No need to increase the image size for those who don't use it.

@keith-packard compared to your PR I did not remove support for constructors on the arc MWDT toolchain.
I added your signoff to my first commit for attribution.

> It looks like CONFIG_CPP_STATIC_INIT_GNU is not being properly deprecated.

@stephanosio I deprecated it now. But being as it was an internal option my understanding was that it was not necessary.
Please re-review.
